SUMMARY:[Time Series & Sequential Data][Machine Learning] FMTS @ NeurIPS 20
 26 - Workshop paper submission deadline
DESCRIPTION:Conference title: Foundation Models for Temporal Systems: From 
 Forecasting to World Modeling\nWebsite: https://fmts-workshop.github.io/\
 nSource URL: https://fmts-workshop.github.io/cfp.html\nLocation: Sydney\,
  Australia\nTopics: Time Series & Sequential Data\, Machine Learning\, De
 ep Representation Learning\, Probabilistic\, Causal & Uncertainty ML\nSiz
 e: S\nSubmission type: Workshop / non-archival short paper\nConfidence: c
 onfirmed\nLast checked date: 2026-10-28\nNotes: NeurIPS's official worksh
 op page lists FMTS on Dec 11\, 2026\, 8:00 AM-5:00 PM AEDT in room MR C4.
 5\; the workshop site still says day TBA. The Sep 16 11:59 UTC (Sep 15 Ao
 E) paper deadline has passed. The Nov 6 camera-ready date is still marked
  tentative and is not listed as a deadline.\nScope: Foundation models for
  temporal systems\, centered on long-horizon and probabilistic forecastin
 g\, temporal pretraining\, generative simulation\, irregularly sampled an
 d multimodal sequences\, and state-space architectures. Reliability is a 
 defining theme: distribution shift\, calibrated uncertainty\, leakage-awa
 re benchmarks\, and consistency of simulated trajectories.\nAdditional to
 pics: System Identification & Data-driven Dynamics\, Robustness & Safety\
 nScope sources (2026): https://fmts-workshop.github.io/cfp.html\nScope la
 st checked: 2026-10-07
URL:https://fmts-workshop.github.io/cfp.html
